# An exact uint64 sum or product past 2^64-1 never wraps to zero: with a
# positive operand it is a nonzero divisor, printed or returned as `int`.
a=(x:uint64 m:uint64<(>? 0)>):>void => printl(7 % (x + m))
c=(x:uint64 m:uint64<(>? 0)>):>int => 7 // (x + m)
d=(y:uint64<(>? 0)> z:uint64<(>? 0)>):>int => 9 % (y * z)
e=(x:uint64):>int => 100 // (x + 1)
main=()=>{
    a(18446744073709551615 1)
    a(3 1)
    printl(c(1 2))
    printl(c(18446744073709551615 18446744073709551615))
    printl(d(2 3))
    printl(e(18446744073709551615))
    printl(e(3))
}
